  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is allowed to oscillate near the point of minima of a vertical parabolic path having the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></math>&nbsp;is along the horizontal direction and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></math>&nbsp;is along the vertical direction. The angular frequency of small oscillations of the particle is</p>\r"
